        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-73104d59b2@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-73104d59b2@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Mar 22 2023 13:32:34 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><span class=\"futura-bold\">Kalamazoo, Michigan, USA</span> — Stryker, one of the world's leading medical technology companies, announced the Xpedition powered stair chair. Improving on the original stair chair, the Xpedition includes increased comfort and security for both the patient and the first responder team.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&quot;We are thrilled to announce our latest innovation in patient transport, the Xpedition powered stair chair. This chair was designed with our customers to provide a safer solution going up and down stairs, as well as improving the overall transport experience for both patients and caregivers,&quot; said Anne Mullally, Vice President and General Manager of Stryker's Emergency Care business. “We are really excited to get this latest innovation into the hands of our customers.”&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Key features and benefits of the Xpedition include:&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Designed to decrease the risk of patient and caregiver injury when moving patients up and downstairs on the durable power track, no lifting required.</li>\n<li>A secure patient containment system to help reduce patient safety concerns and increase physical/psychological security.</li>\n<li>Larger seat pan area for patient comfort while maintaining the same folder storage footprint as Stryker's Stair-PRO stair chair.</li>\n<li>Intuitive user interface with backlit indicator buttons and bright lights.</li>\n<li>Front and back LED lights to increase visibility.</li>\n<li>Designed to help prevent damage to staircases with a flexible belt that conforms to stairs for maximum traction.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Xpedition joins an impressive lineup of powered transport products at Stryker including the Power-PRO 2 powered ambulance cot and the Power-LOAD powered cot fastener.&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Mar 22 2023 13:34:45 GMT+0000",
